Rudroid contribution policy

First-party contributions use the Rudroid Noncommercial Source-Share License
1.0 in the root LICENSE. Commercial use is prohibited; distribution or network
access requires public corresponding source and the same terms for derivatives.
By knowingly submitting a contribution for inclusion, you offer your original
material under those terms. You retain copyright; no assignment is implied.
You must have authority to provide the applicable copyright and patent rights.

For reused code and dependencies, identify their original source, version,
copyright holders, license and modifications. Preserve their original notices
and verify compatibility before inclusion. A reference to another implementation
is not permission to copy its protected code. Do not relabel third-party GPL
material as noncommercial without the necessary copyright permission.

Before distributing binaries or providing network access, prepare the matching
complete source, build instructions, LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES,
including optional native dependency notices. Provide the public source location
required by LICENSE. Private local modifications do not have to be published.
